{"availability":"available","full":"DrEvil-TitaniumHelix/vsav-engine","name":"vsav-engine","description":"VALOR Engine (VASSAL-Adjudicated Legality Of Rules): encodes printed wargames whole - map, counters, rules, combat tables - behind a deterministic legality gate with seeded dice and replay-verifiable logs. Five games incl. AI opponents. Play in the browser: https://vassal-test.pages.dev","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":6,"forks":2,"created":"2026-07-02T21:04:27Z","updated":"2026-09-22T20:31:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://vassal-test.pages.dev","topics":[],"demo":"https://vassal-test.pages.dev/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:42:49.187Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T11:42:49.187Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T11:42:49.187Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T08:58:45.940Z","stars":6,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-12T11:42:49.187Z","stars":6,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["▶ Play it in your browser — nothing to install:","(Formerly \"Dr Evil's Game Legality Engine for VASSAL\". The repo keeps its vsav-engine slug; the system is the VALOR Engine.)","This system encodes a printed wargame whole — the map, the counters, the rules, the combat tables — and makes it a computerized version of the game. Not a digital tabletop where you push pieces and consult the rulebook yourself: the game itself, encoded. The map becomes grid geometry and per-hex terrain; every counter becomes data with its factors and its art; every rule becomes an enforced procedure citing its rulebook section; every combat table is transcribed cell by cell and rolled on by the engine. The result plays like the printed game because it is the printed game, executable."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/DrEvil-TitaniumHelix/vsav-engine/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"b99a64ef7072cc0e8aee802240d61ab46587695b4d5b5a48520dbbdd5e1905d5","extractedAt":"2026